# TypeScript conventions

`any` is banned by ESLint (`@typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any`). Do not add disable comments to work around it.

## Untrusted external data

Treat external data as untrusted (API responses, FormData, search params, cookies, third-party payloads). Validate it at the appropriate boundary with an existing Zod schema or a suitable runtime check before use.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — trust the shape of external JSON
const trip = (await res.json()) as Trip

// ✅ GOOD — validate at the boundary
const trip = tripSchema.parse(await res.json())
```

Prefer reusing feature schemas under `schemas/` over one-off casts or hand-rolled guards when a schema already exists.

## Return types — infer by default

Prefer inferred return types when TypeScript can infer them clearly. Do not add an explicit return type just because a function is exported.

Add an explicit return type when it clarifies a public contract, resolves recursive/blocked inference, or constrains a non-obvious API.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — exported alone is not a reason for an explicit return type
export function formatTripLabel(trip: Trip): string {
  return `${trip.destination} · ${trip.days}d`
}

// ✅ GOOD — inference is clear
export function formatTripLabel(trip: Trip) {
  return `${trip.destination} · ${trip.days}d`
}

// ✅ GOOD — explicit when it constrains a contract or recursive inference
export function getSession(): Promise<Session | null> {
  return loadSession()
}
```

## Object types and component props

Prefer `interface` over `type` for object shapes. Use `type` for unions, intersections used as aliases, and mapped types.

Exception: the primary component in a file MUST use a file-local `type Props = { ... }` (not `interface Props`, not an exported `*Props` name unless the component is shared across files).

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
export interface TripCardProps {
  trip: Trip
  onOpen: (id: string) => void
}

// ✅ GOOD — file-local Props for the primary component
type Props = {
  trip: Trip
  onOpen: (id: string) => void
}

export function TripCard({ trip, onOpen }: Props) {
  return <button onClick={() => onOpen(trip.id)}>{trip.name}</button>
}

// ✅ GOOD — interface for shared object shapes; type for unions/mapped types
interface Trip {
  id: string
  name: string
}

type TripStatus = 'draft' | 'planned' | 'archived'
type Flags = { [K in TripStatus]?: boolean }
```
